## 🎮 Game Creation Patterns

### 🎯 Core Principle
**Never manually handle timestamps when creating games in UI code.** The data layer should manage all timestamp concerns automatically.

### ✅ For UI Code (Recommended)
Use these patterns when creating games from user interfaces, forms, or user interactions:

#### Preferred: Provider Convenience Method
```dart
// Best for UI code - automatically handles timestamps and IDs
ref.read(gameListProvider.notifier).createGame(
  title: 'New Game',
  platform: 'PC',
  status: GameStatus.backlog,
  imagePath: '/optional/image/path.jpg',
  remoteImageUrl: 'https://optional.com/image.jpg',
);
```

#### Alternative: Factory Constructor
```dart
// Also acceptable for UI - creates game with auto-timestamps
final game = GameItem.create(
  title: 'New Game',
  platform: 'PC',
  status: GameStatus.backlog,
);
ref.read(gameListProvider.notifier).addGame(game);
```

### 🏗️ For Data Layer (When Needed)
Use this pattern when you need to preserve specific timestamps (imports, migrations, etc.):

```dart
// When you need to preserve specific timestamps
final gameWithSpecificTimestamps = GameItem(
  id: GameId.generate(), // or existing ID
  title: 'Imported Game',
  platform: 'Switch',
  status: GameStatus.playing,
  lastModified: importTimestamp,      // Preserve original
  lastStatusChange: importTimestamp,  // Preserve original
);
ref.read(gameListProvider.notifier).addGame(gameWithSpecificTimestamps);
```

### 📋 Usage Guidelines

#### ✅ Do
- **UI Code**: Always use `createGame()` or `GameItem.create()`
- **Data Layer**: Use full `GameItem()` constructor only when preserving timestamps
- **Import/Migration**: Use `addGame()` with explicit timestamps
- **Tests**: Use appropriate method based on what you're testing

#### ❌ Don't
- Manually set `DateTime.now()` in UI code
- Use full `GameItem()` constructor in UI without good reason
- Mix timestamp handling approaches in the same feature
- Forget to test both creation patterns

### 🧪 Testing Patterns

#### Testing UI Game Creation
```dart
// Test the convenience method
container.read(gameListProvider.notifier).createGame(
  title: 'Test Game',
  platform: 'PC',
  status: GameStatus.backlog,
);

// Verify timestamps are current
final games = container.read(gameListProvider);
final newGame = games.last;
expect(newGame.lastModified.isAfter(beforeCreate), true);
```

#### Testing Data Layer Preservation
```dart
// Test timestamp preservation
final specificTime = DateTime(2023, 5, 15);
final game = GameItem(
  id: GameId.generate(),
  title: 'Preserved Game',
  platform: 'PC',
  status: GameStatus.playing,
  lastModified: specificTime,
  lastStatusChange: specificTime,
);
container.read(gameListProvider.notifier).addGame(game);

// Verify timestamps are preserved
final games = container.read(gameListProvider);
final addedGame = games.firstWhere((g) => g.id == game.id);
expect(addedGame.lastModified, specificTime);
```

## 🚀 Enforcement

- All new widgets must follow these patterns
- Use existing widgets as reference implementations
- Extract complex build methods during code reviews
- **Mandatory testing** for all new widgets and significant changes
- **Quality gates** - Code must pass analyze and tests before merge
- Always add tests when building new functionality

